{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/639158-da-fae-in-modern-era","id":639158,"title":"DA: Fae in Modern Era","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-25T09:24:55-07:00","id":639158,"title":"DA: Fae in Modern Era","content":"For those who don't like Changeling: The Dreaming and want to find a alternative Fae game to play although there's Changeling: The Lost even though it's NWoD and there's DA: Fae but the only problem however that it's strictly set during the Middle Ages which what if I wanted to play the Modern Ages but I don't want to play Dreaming? Therefore I think it's why DA: Fae should be offered as a alternative...<br /> <br /> Of course the only question remains is, how do you make DA: Fae work in the modern era and has anyone tried it? Although personally, I hope OynxPath considers the possibility of releasing more DA: Fae material in the future especially making a supplement about setting it in modern times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T11:48:49-07:00","id":639335,"title":"","content":"They wouldn't make a supplement setting it in the present, because that would be Changeling. It'd be easy enough to see DA: Fae in the present however. Just take DA: Fae, ignore all the sections on the Mediaeval setting, and set it now. Hey presto!<br /> <br /> Character creation, magic, etc, could all stay the same. The only difference would be where and when you set it, and whether you decide that fae have some kind of masquerade (or whether or not to port in the Mists).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T22:27:59-07:00","id":641141,"title":"","content":"I did something like that once took part of the story from the dreaming and mixed it in. The mists hide some things but it's more people justify and forget things than never see them. Echoes exist often modified to modern effects. <br /> <br /> The idea of the setting was that at the end of the dark ages with magic fading the first born and most of the other fae retired to the fairy realms to continue there battles and escape the world that feared them and the church that destroys them.<br /> <br /> Jump forward to the return but it's a slower return and the paths to deep fairy are opened but very dangerous and as you get deeper into fairy you may find time very different. So the moon landing and the first born return along with many changelings and inanimate who had lived in fairy to find that changlings still live on earth and most have undergone a ritual that traded there single immortal life for many human ones a ritual that also greatly protects them from echos, the changeling way.<br /> <br /> quite the opposite of changeling the dreaming the theme is actual the return of magic but also possibly the return of madness and though the church is no longer the force it once was forging oaths and finding a way to live with and around the mortals who no longer believe in or fear then is a struggle especially for those newly returned to whom the mortal world and it's technology is strange and unknown. As well as keeping in check the long dormant and recently returned magical creatures and effects in the world. Plus the old struggles between noble and commoner and the various courts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:39:25-07:00","id":644632,"title":"","content":"We have incorporated DA:Fae into our VtM games. The only difference being that new Fae are rarely born in the modern age, so they are incredibly rare and a bit reclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}